  "completionAndEvidenceChecks": [
    "Producer checkpoint requires natural success of required configure/configuration/export/Rust/archive stages, every prior owned leader exactly reaped with zero status, verified gone groups, no cleanup failure or first/monitor failure, and available untruncated sampled birth history.",
    "Fresh self-bound full census rejects any known live or zombie build birth independently of its current credentials/group. Unavailable required identity evidence fails; unrelated UID births do not define build ownership or receive implicit zero counters.",
    "Archive and dependency hashes bind the selected successful Rust boundary to the object manifest. Exact descriptor-stream hashing, archive readback and full selected-root rescans must pass before readiness; interrupted state is not eligible.",
    "Upload follows verified ready summary, premeasured archive size/hash and reserved-time checks. The consumer accepts only the same run/attempt successful producer artifact with fixed service/archive/manifest/content/configuration checks.",
    "Build failure excerpts retain bounded classified before-cleanup and after-cleanup observations without changing the primary failure. The fixed context/GUI recorder separately retains pre-cleanup functional failure, reported event cause, host/launcher/child facts and cleanup results with fixed public projection.",
    "The corrected producer and consumer preflights retain non-Runner phase failures, existing first failure, recovered monitor diagnostics and persistence failure without publishing arbitrary exception text."
  ],
  "resolvedFinding": {
    "severity": "P2",
    "issue": "The prior inline preflight could report failed status with null firstFailure for a direct probe/snapshot/count failure, and omitted recovered monitor diagnostics.",
    "resolution": "Both roles now capture a fixed failure code/phase without replacing a preexisting first failure, export monitorDiagnostics, and preserve the primary exception on persistence failure. A persistence-only failure prints failed evidence and raises a fixed failure."
  },
